WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.869
Before we get started, I want

2
00:00:01.869 --> 00:00:03.657
you to know something important.

3
00:00:03.657 --> 00:00:05.550
This isn’t a test, and there

4
00:00:05.550 --> 00:00:07.454
are no right or wrong answers.

5
00:00:07.454 --> 00:00:09.579
We’re not here to judge how you spend your money

6
00:00:09.579 --> 00:00:12.179
or tell you what your budget should look like.

7
00:00:12.179 --> 00:00:15.151
This quick financial stability check simply helps us

8
00:00:15.151 --> 00:00:18.123
understand what’s coming in, what’s going out, and

9
00:00:18.123 --> 00:00:20.573
whether there are expenses or barriers that could

10
00:00:20.573 --> 00:00:22.732
make it harder to reach your employment goals.

11
00:00:23.243 --> 00:00:25.031
What you share can help your career coach

12
00:00:25.031 --> 00:00:28.085
identify support services that may be available to

13
00:00:28.085 --> 00:00:31.335
help you move forward —things like transportation, work

14
00:00:31.335 --> 00:00:35.712
clothing, tools, childcare, or other employment- related needs.

15
00:00:35.712 --> 00:00:38.882
Participation in this financial check- in is voluntary.

16
00:00:38.882 --> 00:00:42.376
However, if you are requesting support services, it must

17
00:00:42.376 --> 00:00:45.244
be completed before those services can be issued.

18
00:00:45.244 --> 00:00:47.345
Just give us your best estimate.

19
00:00:47.345 --> 00:00:49.145
It doesn’t have to be perfect.

20
00:00:49.145 --> 00:00:50.468
The goal is simple:

21
00:00:50.468 --> 00:00:52.964
understand where things stand today, identify

22
00:00:52.964 --> 00:00:54.532
what might help, and keep you

23
00:00:54.532 --> 00:00:56.378
moving toward your employment goals.
